        "GOLDILOCKS": {
            "name": "Goldilocks Principle",
            "abbreviation": "GOLDILOCKS",
            "originator": "Berlyne, 1971 (originator); Kirsh, 2026 (extended to architectural cognition and cross-sensory universality)",
            "phenomena_organized": "Cross-modal inverted-U optimum for prediction error across all sensory and architectural dimensions. Extended from Berlyne's visual-complexity aesthetics to a universal PE optimization mechanism operating across noise tolerance, visual complexity, thermal comfort, spiciness, and more. Critically, the Goldilocks curve is culturally sensitive — different cultures exhibit different optima for tolerable ambient noise, visual complexity, spiciness of food, and many other dimensions.",
